Z||000000||fierobaby||08-02-2001||02:10 AM||||ok I'm sure you guys are sick of hearing about my brakes....problem is now I am stuck doing them myself... I know little about cars...but would love to learn.... I will try to figure out how far my father got.... doesn't look to far though.... but so far I know we have to put in at least 2 brake lines.... so any help anyone could offer would be awesome...if anyone wants to come help me I'd love you for life...<P><BR>Corinne<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="LETTER"> AIM: Fierobaby87<BR>http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero </FONT><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-02-2001||08:13 AM||||I recently replaced everything on my brakes, lines,calibers,rotors,etc..<P>Check out your local parts store and see if any of them have tool rentals/loans ..<P>I just got the steel lines on a roll, and reused my couplings and flanged my ends myself with a ISO(double) flange tool I borrowed as a loaner tool.<P> If you dont have access to a loaner tool, buy the correct lenths, bend to the right shape (I had a pipe bender but found it easier to bend by hand) and take it to a carpart store and get them to flange them for you.<P>If you have a few rusty lines.. for safety sake, you may want to change them all.. A few of my lines looked ok, but after getting them off..I'm sure glad I did..   Last thing you would want is to have them bust..<P> good luck!<P><BR>edited for typos  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
